<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Parleq Sparkle appcast.

  Served at https://parleq.app/appcast.xml (configured as
  SUFeedURL in parleq-app/Resources/Info.plist). Sparkle on
  installed Parleq builds fetches this file on launch + on a
  ~24h timer and prompts the user when the latest item below
  describes a newer version than the running build.

  Each item's sparkle:edSignature is an Ed25519 signature over
  the linked .dmg's bytes, produced by Sparkle's sign_update
  tool against the maintainer's private key. The matching
  public key ships inside every Parleq build via Info.plist's
  SUPublicEDKey. Sparkle refuses any update whose enclosure
  signature doesn't verify against that exact public key, so a
  downstream attacker who swaps either the appcast file or the
  .dmg cannot push an arbitrary binary to existing installs.

  Items are inserted automatically by make release. The
  insertion marker is the single-line HTML comment immediately
  below the language element inside the channel. New entries
  land directly below that marker line, so the top of the
  channel is always the freshest release and older entries get
  pushed downward.

  Do not paraphrase the literal marker token anywhere else in
  this file — the Makefile's awk matcher looks for that exact
  string and would otherwise insert items inside this
  documentation block (which is itself a comment, so they'd be
  ignored by Sparkle entirely). The marker is intentionally
  positioned on a single line outside this comment so awk
  insertion lands as a proper element child of <channel>.
-->
